# The evidence

How do we know these gods were worshipped, and since when? Three kinds of
evidence: their names on the clay tablets of the Mycenaean palaces, the
sanctuaries where they had cult, and the texts that tell their myths.

Each kind is a module of `lib/myth/` that implements the trait `Evidence`:
the trait declares `subject`, `dated`, `kind` and `reference` without a
body, and each module supplies them for its own type. `Witness` is the
union of the three types, so one list holds every piece of evidence.

```hql id=ev hidden
import myth.kb
import myth.beings
import myth.tablets
import myth.sites
import myth.evidence

witnesses = evidence.witnesses()
first = (being: String, kind: String) => evidence.earliest(witnesses, being, kind).unwrap_or("")

{
    tablets: evidence.tablets()
        | map(t => {tablet: t.id, palace: t.site, god: kb.name(t.being), form: t.form, syllabary: t.glyphs(), secure: t.secure, note: t.note})
        | Table(columns = ["tablet", "palace", "god", "form", "syllabary", "secure", "note"]),
    sites: evidence.sites()
        | sort(by = s => s.year)
        | map(s => {site: s.name, place: s.place, god: kb.name(s.being), date: s.dating, note: s.note})
        | Table(columns = ["site", "place", "god", "date", "note"]),
    first: kb.beings()
        | filter(b => b.olympian() or b.id == "hestia" or b.id == "hades" or b.id == "heracles")
        | map(b => {god: b.name, earliest: first(b.id, ""), first_text: first(b.id, "text")})
        | Table(columns = ["god", "earliest", "first_text"]),
}
```

All three tables are built in the hidden cell above, the one cell of this
document that imports the evidence modules; the cells below write them.

## Linear B

Linear B is the script of the Mycenaean palaces, deciphered by Michael
Ventris in 1952 as the earliest written Greek. The tablets survive because
the fires that destroyed the palaces baked them: Knossos around 1375 BCE,
Pylos around 1200. Several Olympians are named on them, five centuries
before Homer. The syllabary column is written by the `greek` package from
the transliteration.

```hql#eval
ev.tablets
```
<!-- hql:output hash=fc4e7bf337c2 status=ok -->
"Table([{form: \"di-ka-ta-jo di-we\", god: \"Zeus\", note: \"oil to Diktaian Zeus\", palace: \"Knossos\", secure: true, syllabary: \"𐀇𐀏𐀲𐀍𐄀𐀇𐀸\", tablet: \"KN Fp 1\"}, {form: \"e-ri-nu\", god: \"Erinyes\", note: \"oil to Erinys\", palace: \"Knossos\", secure: true, syllabary: \"𐀁𐀪𐀝\", tablet: \"KN Fp 1\"}, {form: \"a-ta-na-po-ti-ni-ja\", god: \"Athena\", note: \"read as 'Mistress of Atana'; whether this is Athena is debated\", palace: \"Knossos\", secure: false, syllabary: \"𐀀𐀲𐀙𐀡𐀴𐀛𐀊\", tablet: \"KN V 52\"}, {form: \"e-nu-wa-ri-jo\", god: \"Ares\", note: \"Enyalios, later an epithet of Ares\", palace: \"Knossos\", secure: false, syllabary: \"𐀁𐀝𐀷𐀪𐀍\", tablet: \"KN V 52\"}, {form: \"pa-ja-wo-ne\", god: \"Apollo\", note: \"Paiawon, later Paean, an epithet of Apollo\", palace: \"Knossos\", secure: false, syllabary: \"𐀞𐀊𐀺𐀚\", tablet: \"KN V 52\"}, {form: \"e-re-u-ti-ja\", god: \"Eileithyia\", note: \"honey to Eileithyia at Amnisos\", palace: \"Knossos\", secure: true, syllabary: \"𐀁𐀩𐀄𐀴𐀊\", tablet: \"KN Gg 705\"}, {form: \"a-pa-i-ti-jo\", god: \"Hephaestus\", note: \"a man's name, Haphaistios, derived from the god's\", palace: \"Knossos\", secure: false, syllabary: \"𐀀𐀞𐀂𐀴𐀍\", tablet: \"KN L 588\"}, {form: \"di-wo-nu-so\", god: \"Dionysus\", note: \"honey to Zeus and Dionysus\", palace: \"Chania\", secure: true, syllabary: \"𐀇𐀺𐀝𐀰\", tablet: \"KH Gq 5\"}, {form: \"di-we\", god: \"Zeus\", note: \"a vessel and a man to Zeus\", palace: \"Pylos\", secure: true, syllabary: \"𐀇𐀸\", tablet: \"PY Tn 316\"}, {form: \"e-ra\", god: \"Hera\", note: \"a vessel and a woman to Hera\", palace: \"Pylos\", secure: true, syllabary: \"𐀁𐀨\", tablet: \"PY Tn 316\"}, {form: \"e-ma-a2\", god: \"Hermes\", note: \"a vessel and a man to Hermes\", palace: \"Pylos\", secure: true, syllabary: \"𐀁𐀔𐁀\", tablet: \"PY Tn 316\"}, {form: \"po-se-da-o-ne\", god: \"Poseidon\", note: \"grain, wine, a bull and cheeses to Poseidon\", palace: \"Pylos\", secure: true, syllabary: \"𐀡𐀮𐀅𐀃𐀚\", tablet: \"PY Un 718\"}, {form: \"a-te-mi-to\", god: \"Artemis\", note: \"a slave of Artemis\", palace: \"Pylos\", secure: true, syllabary: \"𐀀𐀳𐀖𐀵\", tablet: \"PY Es 650\"}, {form: \"da-ma-te\", god: \"Demeter\", note: \"read by some as Demeter, by others as a word for household land\", palace: \"Pylos\", secure: false, syllabary: \"𐀅𐀔𐀳\", tablet: \"PY En 609\"}], columns = [\"tablet\", \"palace\", \"god\", \"form\", \"syllabary\", \"secure\", \"note\"])"
