## Sanctuaries

Places of cult, oldest first.

```hql#eval
ev.sites
```
<!-- hql:output hash=8ac7b3fcc073 status=ok -->
"Table([{date: \"c. 1200 BCE\", god: \"Aphrodite\", note: \"Aphrodite goes to her precinct and altar at Paphos, Odyssey 8.362–363\", place: \"Palaepaphos, Cyprus\", site: \"Sanctuary of Aphrodite\"}, {date: \"first temple 8th century BCE\", god: \"Hera\", note: \"Herodotus 3.60 calls its later temple the largest he knew\", place: \"Samos\", site: \"Heraion of Samos\"}, {date: \"sanctuary from the 8th century BCE\", god: \"Apollo\", note: \"the standing temple is of the 4th century BCE\", place: \"Delphi\", site: \"Sanctuary of Apollo\"}, {date: \"c. 690–650 BCE\", god: \"Poseidon\", note: \"one of the earliest monumental temples in Greece; seat of the Isthmian Games\", place: \"Isthmia\", site: \"Temple of Poseidon\"}, {date: \"c. 600 BCE\", god: \"Hera\", note: \"the Hermes of Praxiteles was found in it in 1877\", place: \"Olympia\", site: \"Temple of Hera\"}, {date: \"c. 600 BCE\", god: \"Apollo\", note: \"a Naxian dedication in the sanctuary of Apollo's birthplace\", place: \"Delos\", site: \"Terrace of the Lions\"}, {date: \"c. 560–550 BCE\", god: \"Artemis\", note: \"Croesus gave most of its columns, Herodotus 1.92; burned in 356 BCE; its rebuilt successor was counted among the Seven Wonders\", place: \"Ephesus\", site: \"Temple of Artemis\"}, {date: \"lead oracle tablets 6th–3rd century BCE\", god: \"Zeus\", note: \"Achilles prays to Zeus of Dodona, Iliad 16.233–235\", place: \"Dodona\", site: \"Oracle of Zeus\"}, {date: \"c. 470–456 BCE\", god: \"Zeus\", note: \"held the gold-and-ivory Zeus of Pheidias, c. 435 BCE\", place: \"Olympia\", site: \"Temple of Zeus\"}, {date: \"c. 460 BCE\", god: \"Heracles\", note: \"the twelve labours, six over each porch\", place: \"Olympia\", site: \"Metopes of the Temple of Zeus\"}, {date: \"c. 450–400 BCE\", god: \"Apollo\", note: \"Pausanias 8.41.9 names Iktinos as its architect\", place: \"Bassae\", site: \"Temple of Apollo Epikourios\"}, {date: \"c. 449–415 BCE\", god: \"Hephaestus\", note: \"the best-preserved Doric temple in Greece\", place: \"Athens\", site: \"Temple of Hephaestus\"}, {date: \"447–432 BCE\", god: \"Athena\", note: \"its west pediment showed the contest with Poseidon, Pausanias 1.24.5\", place: \"Athens\", site: \"Parthenon\"}, {date: \"c. 444–440 BCE\", god: \"Poseidon\", note: \"on the cape at the southern tip of Attica\", place: \"Sounion\", site: \"Temple of Poseidon\"}, {date: \"c. 440 BCE\", god: \"Ares\", note: \"moved to the Agora and rebuilt there in the late 1st century BCE\", place: \"Athens\", site: \"Temple of Ares\"}, {date: \"rebuilt in the 5th century BCE\", god: \"Demeter\", note: \"on the site of the temple the Hymn to Demeter has her command, lines 270–274, and of the rites she teaches, 473–479\", place: \"Eleusis\", site: \"Telesterion\"}, {date: \"stone theatre c. 330 BCE\", god: \"Dionysus\", note: \"the Bacchae was first staged here in 405 BCE, in the theatre as it was before the stone rebuilding\", place: \"Athens\", site: \"Theatre of Dionysus Eleuthereus\"}], columns = [\"site\", \"place\", \"god\", \"date\", \"note\"])"
